{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2186-06-30 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. ___ . I'm Dr. ___, part of your care team. You're here today for your 20th cycle of high-dose methotrexate as part of reinduction therapy for your CNS lymphoma."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2186-06-30 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good morning, Doctor. Yes, I’ve been doing this for a while now. I feel okay—just the usual tinnitus. But I did forget my desmopressin this morning. Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2186-06-30 09:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You take desmopressin for your diabetes insipidus. We’ll keep an eye on your sodium levels, especially with all the IV fluids you’ll get during chemo. For now, we’ll give you your dose later today as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2186-06-30 09:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I just don’t want it to cause any problems."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2186-06-30 09:19:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We monitor that closely. Your labs this morning look stable—sodium is 136, which is good. We’ll check it again tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2186-06-30 09:20:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. And I brought my Temodar—I started it at home yesterday as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2186-06-30 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’ll continue that here for seven days on, seven off. We’ll also give you ondansetron before each dose to help prevent nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2186-06-30 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been taking it IV at home when needed. Is it okay to switch to oral?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2186-06-30 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll switch to oral ondansetron starting today. It’s just as effective and easier for you long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2186-06-30 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. I’ve been managing pretty well overall."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2186-06-30 11:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re about to start your methotrexate infusion. It’ll take a few hours. We’ve alkalinized your urine to protect your kidneys, and you’ll get leucovorin rescue starting tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2186-06-30 11:46:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. It helps reduce side effects, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2186-06-30 11:47:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It ‘rescues’ your healthy cells from the chemo. You’re getting 8 grams per square meter, which for you is about 19,520 mg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2186-06-30 11:48:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a big dose. But I’ve done it before—hope I tolerate it well again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2186-06-30 11:49:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "So far, so good. We’ll monitor you closely. Let us know if you feel nauseous or have any pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2186-06-30 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, I’ve been urinating a lot since the fluids started. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2186-06-30 14:31:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s expected. The IV fluids and your desmopressin can interact. We’re watching your sodium because of your diabetes insipidus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2186-06-30 14:32:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ah, right. You mentioned that earlier. Should I still take my next desmopressin dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2186-06-30 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll hold the afternoon dose today. Your sodium dropped to 132, which is mildly low. By holding desmopressin, we let your body clear excess water. We’ll recheck in the morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2186-06-30 14:35:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust your judgment. I just want to stay safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2186-07-01 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your sodium is now 135 and trending up. You had a good amount of urine output, which means the adjustment worked."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2186-07-01 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Can I restart my regular desmopressin schedule?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2186-07-01 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll resume your usual three times daily dosing. Your methotrexate level is also coming down as expected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2186-07-01 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What should it be at this point?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2186-07-01 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was 0.09 this morning, which is excellent. It needs to drop below 0.1 before we stop leucovorin. You’re right on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2186-07-01 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. And my other meds—everything’s continuing as usual?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2186-07-01 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your lisinopril, sertraline, and Keppra are all being given. No changes there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2186-07-01 09:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been sleeping okay with the trazodone when I need it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2186-07-01 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also got your chest CT from earlier. It shows some old changes from past TB exposure, but nothing active or new."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2186-07-01 11:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Because of my mom’s history?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2186-07-01 11:32:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You’re at higher risk, so we always take precautions, like the negative pressure room. But the scan looks stable—no signs of reactivation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2186-07-01 11:33:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I was worried about that with the chemo weakening my system."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2186-07-01 11:34:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We are too, which is why we monitor closely. Your abdominal CT also showed no signs of lymphoma or TB there—just a small stable adrenal nodule."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2186-07-01 11:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Nothing unexpected then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2186-07-01 11:37:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, everything looks as expected. You’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2186-07-02 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning, Mr. ___. You’re ready for discharge. Your methotrexate level is 0.09, sodium is 137, and you’re feeling well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2186-07-02 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2186-07-02 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’ll finish your leucovorin at home—45 mg every six hours for a few more doses. Then stop. Resume all your usual meds, including desmopressin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2186-07-02 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And Temodar continues as planned?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2186-07-02 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, keep taking it daily for five more days. Then you’ll have a break before the next cycle. You’ll see the oncology team in clinic for your Rituxan infusion and follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2186-07-02 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I come back here in two weeks for the next methotrexate?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2186-07-02 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. Call us if you develop fever, confusion, or anything unusual before then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2186-07-02 08:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for taking such good care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2186-07-02 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You did well with this cycle. We’ll see you soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2186-06-30 00:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2186-07-02 20:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 65-year-old man with recurrent primary central nervous system lymphoma was admitted for his 20th cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy as part of reinduction therapy. He presented in stable condition, tolerating the infusion well without acute symptoms. His hospital course was complicated by mild hyponatremia (sodium 132), likely due to interaction between intravenous fluids and desmopressin for his diabetes insipidus. This was managed by holding one dose of desmopressin, resulting in improved sodium levels (137 at discharge). Methotrexate levels declined appropriately to 0.09, and leucovorin rescue was administered as planned. He remained neurologically stable, seizure-free, and hemodynamically normal throughout. He was discharged home with instructions to resume all home medications and continue oral leucovorin for a short course, with follow-up scheduled in clinic for Rituxan and planning for the next chemotherapy cycle.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Primary central nervous system lymphoma, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Diabetes insipidus",
      "Other disorders of neurohypophysis",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, without mention of intractable epilepsy",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified"
    ]
  }
}
